# FlutterFlow edit vs instruct

This app is a FlutterFlow project. FlutterFlow regenerates `lib/pages` (and page models). Local edits there are overwritten on Local Run, Pull Latest, or regenerate.

## Edit these (then user Pushes via VS Code)

- `lib/custom_code/actions/**`
- `lib/custom_code/widgets/**`
- `lib/flutter_flow/custom_functions.dart` when needed
- Keep FlutterFlow headers (`DO NOT REMOVE OR MODIFY THE CODE ABOVE`).

## Do not edit — give manual FlutterFlow steps

- `lib/pages/**` (Wait Page, Dashboard, Slot Selection, all `*_widget.dart` / `*_model.dart`)
- Other builder-generated UI (`lib/components` page-like generated widgets)

Numbered builder steps: which page, which action, order, await vs parallel. Never patch `*_widget.dart`.

## Other

- Durable logic belongs in Custom Actions (`setupFCMListener`, `synFCMToken`, `mirrorMatchingDataToRTDB`, etc.).
- Match FCM send path uses only `appStats/{uid}/f` (all slots in that node).
- Leftover Cloud Functions: paste-ready JS and which folder to deploy. Do not `firebase deploy` listed 23 from `v2-run`.
- Do not edit FlutterFlow roaming copies under `%AppData%/Roaming/FlutterFlow/` to “fix” pages.
